  "slug": "untitled-topic-e003",
  "summary": "Preprints pair nonreciprocal isolators and Floquet metasurfaces with tunable magnonic, ENZ and THz platforms for compact control of optical response.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is control of wave response beyond static, reciprocal behavior in compact geometries. Two items address nonreciprocity directly: a computational study of integrated isolators based on nonreciprocal 2D semiconductors with spin-momentum locking, including an all-optical isolator proposal, and Floquet metasurfaces of three closely spaced conducting sheets that show asymmetric frequency conversion and a reported violation of Kirchhoff's law. Tunability appears elsewhere: a CrCl3 tripartite van der Waals cavity magnonic device with hierarchical anti-crossing and reduced magnon loss, VCMA-driven parametric spin-wave excitation with two phase states, high-Q THz flatbands in Mie-grating metasurfaces, and inverse-designed epsilon-near-zero oxide cavities with stronger confinement. A review covers strain-driven THz phase modulation. The items differ in method and maturity (computational, theoretical, experimental) and do not share one mechanism; the acoustic bound-state study is a wave-physics analogue.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
